        "id": 1531147
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T19:25:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No concern with host timeouts. CONFIG_HOSTCMD_RATE_LIMITING_RECESS is 20 ms (include/config.h). The Linux kernel ChromeOS EC driver (drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_proto.c) timeout is 1000 ms (1 second). Holding off host_send_response() by 20 ms cleanly forces the host LPC/eSPI driver to wait within its timeout window, allowing lower-priority EC tasks (HOOK_TICK at 10 ms, watchdog reload) to execute.\n\n(Drafted with AI assistant on behalf of Jon Murphy)",
      "parentUuid": "9f698192_836c00a9",
